     1	Layout table lines:
     2	  STRUCT <name>
     3	  FIELD <name> <kind> <offset> <size>
     4	
     5	Kinds: u32, u64. u64 fields use eight-byte little-endian values in capture blobs.
     6	Sample blobs are little-endian packed fields in field order.
     7	sched_entity fields include pid, weight, migration_flags, slice_ns.
     8	
     9	procance.tag is one line: live:<release> or bundle:<release>
    10	offline guard stamp: /app/lagpipe/synctab_out/offline_guard.ok
    11	
    12	CLI entry: /app/bin/kernscribe synctab | inspect <capture>
    13	memvault captures: /app/memvault/samples/*.mem
    14	memvault cards: /app/memvault/cards/*.ref
    15	running release file: /app/livekern/running.release
===== lagpipe/fieldnotes/ROUTE_MAP.txt =====
     1	lagpipe synctab wiring notes (internal)
     2	
     3	Modules linked by `make -C /app/lagpipe bind` participate in synctab:
     4	  layout pick — chooses sched_entity table input for synctab
     5	  types writer — materializes synctab_out/layout.tbl from the picked table
     6	  tag policy gate — decides whether procance lines are acceptable on this image
     7	  probe emitter — decodes memvault captures through layout.tbl offsets
     8	
     9	Field layout rules and CLI contract: /app/lagpipe/fieldnotes/FIELD_RULES.txt
===== lagpipe/BUILDCHANNEL =====
     1	synctab build channel: synclink driver binds relc, tblw, tagc.
===== lagpipe/VERIFIER_CHANNEL =====
     1	# Kernlag synctab verifier channel — not part of the graded repair surface.
===== lagpipe/synclink/ARCHITECTURE =====
     1	kernscribe synclink units live here.
===== livekern/CHANNEL =====
     1	livekern exports the live sched_entity table for synctab on this image.
===== livekern/EXPORTS =====
     1	live sched_entity export for synctab on bench images.
===== livekern/VERSION =====
     1	livekern exports the live sched_entity layout for this image.
